From 1659bcf59c0ed633d465441c93797779fba1b9e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:52:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] doc: wallet notification worker

List the per-wallet b-walletnotify thread, and note in the release notes
that wallet callbacks no longer run on the validation scheduler thread,
that unloadwallet waits for queued notifications, and that a wallet
notification failure shuts the node down instead of aborting it.

Tier: eCash
---
 doc/developer-notes.md |  5 +++++
 doc/release-notes.md   | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/developer-notes.md b/doc/developer-notes.md
index c5048b6ab2a0ab7bb9eb8fc2f85bbbe16da0bda7..6710792a3a3adf5bb541e27df5befcbde9efaebb 100644
--- a/doc/developer-notes.md
+++ b/doc/developer-notes.md
@@ -547,6 +547,11 @@ Threads
   : Does asynchronous background tasks like dumping wallet contents, dumping
   addrman and running asynchronous validationinterface callbacks.
 
+- Wallet notification worker (`b-walletnotify`)
+  : One thread per loaded wallet. Delivers that wallet's chain notifications
+  (blocks, mempool transactions, chain state flushes) in validation order, so
+  that a busy wallet does not hold up the scheduler thread.
+
 - [TorControlThread (`b-torcontrol`)](https://www.bitcoinabc.org/doc/dev/torcontrol_8cpp.html#a4faed3692d57a0d7bdbecf3b37f72de0)
   : Boost.Asio thread for the Tor control connection.
 
diff --git a/doc/release-notes.md b/doc/release-notes.md
index aaf9b65f2c248b029317a3120d830bc78f077822..5b2cf3b25a04ddbeb2170aeedf22d6b0045f3c15 100644
--- a/doc/release-notes.md
+++ b/doc/release-notes.md
@@ -5,6 +5,18 @@ Bitcoin ABC version 0.34.1 is now available from:
   <https://download.bitcoinabc.org/0.34.1/>
 
 This release includes the following features and fixes:
+- Wallets receive chain notifications (blocks, mempool transactions and chain
+  state flushes) on a per-wallet worker thread instead of the validation
+  scheduler thread, in the same order as before. A wallet that is busy, for
+  example during a long rescan, no longer delays notifications to the rest of
+  the node until its bounded queue fills. RPCs that wait for wallet
+  notifications (`sendrawtransaction`, `submitpackage` and wallet RPCs that
+  sync to the chain) also wait for this worker.
+- `unloadwallet` now waits until the wallet has processed the notifications
+  already queued for it.
+- An error while a wallet processes a chain notification now shuts the node
+  down cleanly instead of aborting it. The wallet rescans from its last flushed
+  best block on restart.
 - Add new format string placeholders for `walletnotify`:
   - `%b` - the hash of the block containting the transaction (`unconfirmed` if a mempool transaction)
   - `%h` - the height of the block containing the transaction (`-1` if a mempool transaction)
-- 
